


# If a repo is cloned on your computer 
	-> git clone

# Steps:
	Before dev: git pull

	Do your own development 

	After dev: git pull

	git add <filename> or . (current directory) or -A (for all)
		git add -A means all modifications since last commit

	git commit -m "some message" 
		- this is like a checkpoint

	git push -> sends local copy to remote 
